1. uptime command
Purpose: Displays how long the Kali Linux system has been running.

Command:
uptime


Expected output:
18:30:15 up 2 hours, 15 min, 1 user, load average: 0.10, 0.20, 0.15


Your output will show your actual system uptime.
2. date command
Purpose: Displays the current date and time.

Command:
date


Expected output:
Thu Nov 26 18:30:15 IST 2026


Your date and time will be different.
3. mv command
Purpose: Moves a file from one location to another.

Step 1: Create a file
touch file1.txt


Step 2: Create a destination folder
mkdir folder1


Step 3: Move the file
mv file1.txt folder1/


Step 4: Check the moved file
ls folder1


Expected output:
file1.txt
